    ("What is cross-validation?", "Cross-validation splits the data into parts, trains on most of them, and tests on the rest, repeating this multiple times. It gives a more reliable estimate of model performance."),
    ("What is a random forest?", "A random forest is an ensemble of many decision trees. Each tree votes on the answer, and the majority decides, which makes the model more accurate and less prone to overfitting."),
